1
00:04:11,428 --> 00:04:17,428
Why stop making sense? Why a movie? Why a big suit? Where do the
odd movements come from? What will the band do next?

2
00:08:22,857 --> 00:08:28,857
Stop Making Sense is a documentary, music film directed by Jonathan Demme.

3
00:12:34,285 --> 00:12:40,285
A concert film documenting Talking Heads at the height of their popularity, on tour for their 1983 album "Speaking in Tongues." The band takes the stage one by
one and is joined by a cadre of guest musicians for a career-spanning and cinematic performance that features creative choreography and visuals.

4
00:16:45,714 --> 00:16:51,714
Self - Vocals, Guitar, played by David Byrne.

5
00:20:57,142 --> 00:21:03,142
Self - Drums, Vocals, played by Chris Frantz.

6
00:25:08,571 --> 00:25:14,571
Self - Guitar, Keyboards, Vocals, played by Jerry Harrison.

7
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:26,000
Self - Bass, Percussion, Vocals, played by Tina Weymouth.

8
00:33:31,428 --> 00:33:37,428
Self - Backing Vocals, played by Ednah Holt.

9
00:37:42,857 --> 00:37:48,857
Self - Backing Vocals, played by Lynn Mabry.

10
00:41:54,285 --> 00:42:00,285
Stop Making Sense is a 1984 American concert film featuring a live
performance by the American rock band Talking Heads.

11
00:46:05,714 --> 00:46:11,714
The film was directed by Jonathan Demme and executive produced
by Gary Kurfirst, the band’s longtime manager.

12
00:50:17,142 --> 00:50:23,142
The film was shot over four nights in December 1983 at Hollywood’s Pantages Theatre while
Talking Heads were on tour promoting their 1983 album, Speaking in Tongues.

13
00:54:28,571 --> 00:54:34,571
Stop Making Sense includes performances of the early Talking Heads single, "Psycho Killer"
(1977), through to their most recent hit at the time, "Burning Down the House" (1983).

14
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:46,000
It also includes songs from the solo career of frontman David Byrne and by Tom Tom
Club, the side project of drummer Chris Frantz and bassist Tina Weymouth.

15
01:02:51,428 --> 01:02:57,428
The film was independently produced and the band raised
the budget of $1.2 million themselves.

16
01:07:02,857 --> 01:07:08,857
The four core members of Talking Heads are joined by backing singers Lynn Mabry and Ednah Holt,
guitarist Alex Weir, keyboardist Bernie Worrell and percussionist Steve Scales.

17
01:11:14,285 --> 01:11:20,285
Stop Making Sense is considered by many critics to be a classic
and one of the greatest concert films of all time.

18
01:15:25,714 --> 01:15:31,714
The film is a pioneering example of the use of early digital audio techniques.

19
01:19:37,142 --> 01:19:43,142
In 2021, it was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the Library of Congress as being "culturally,
historically, or aesthetically significant." A special 4K restoration of the film was re-released in theaters in September 2023 by A24.

20
01:23:48,571 --> 01:23:54,571
The film explores themes of concert, rock band,
concert film, post-punk, new wave.
